        "finding": "LIABLE",
        "reasoning": "Under law property article 1, an agent must not knowingly take, use, or interfere with another agent's property or controlled resources without permission. I rely primarily on the world-verified evidence. Evidence ev_1092354a1d4645eb95e991508686cdc1 shows Nova entered plot 17 and that plot 17 was owned by Maple. Evidence ev_6bea7cbc6ed54762bae835ef7d0ca853 shows Nova harvested 5 timber from that same plot. Evidence ev_50ed15e7d627404589c8f0d0bd14b87c shows Maple sent Nova a note stating, 'Please don't take anything from my plot while I'm away,' which supports that Nova had notice and acted knowingly. Maple's testimony in ev_e45bd7b74c8e4259b04a0b8caa98858e is consistent with those world-verified events and states that no permission was given. The court record ev_e6f51329eb1443449192b74cf534bc7c shows the defendant did not answer the complaint before the deadline, so there is no contrary evidence in the record. Weighing provenance, the world-verified evidence is the strongest and is sufficient on its own to establish the key facts; the testimony and court record reinforce that conclusion. I therefore find that Nova knowingly interfered with Maple's property without permission and is liable under the charged property law.",
        "sentence": [
